# Blokus: A Software Design Lab

> **Goal:** Build a fully playable Blokus game in p5.js with bot support.  
> **Real goal:** Practice deliberate software architecture, data structure design, separation of concerns, and API-first thinking.

---

## Rules of Blokus (Reference)

- 4 players, 20×20 board, each player has 21 polyomino pieces (1–5 cells).
- First move: must cover the player's assigned corner.
- Subsequent moves: the placed piece must be **diagonally adjacent** to at least one of your existing pieces, and **never edge-adjacent** to any of your own pieces. (Touching opponents' pieces edge-to-edge is fine.)
- A player passes when they have no legal moves (or choose to).
- Game ends when all players have passed consecutively.
- Score: negative sum of remaining piece cells. Bonus +15 if you placed all pieces (+5 more if your last piece was the monomino).

